5863 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435847 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435863 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435863 1077 "selection" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435863 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435847 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435863 1079 #uuid "7bf5e5ce-2a24-563a-8eed-d37940cab8bf" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435834 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435837 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435849 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435854 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435857 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1077 "field-2" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435849 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435864 1079 #uuid "872a01bb-a58c-517b-8a38-5d170114d390" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435865 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435831 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435865 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435833 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435865 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435841 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435865 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435851 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435865 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435865 1077 "field-1" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435865 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435831 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435865 1079 #uuid "db6d7e71-81cf-5a3b-b7fa-5481d846b976" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435866 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435861 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435866 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435862 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435866 1069 "q-339139" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435866 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435866 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y=5,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435866 1072 #uuid "536cae39-f031-5c30-a8b0-a9b62b8632a3" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435866 1074 "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{4}{x}$ and $Q(x)=5.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (4/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y) & ={x}^{4}\\cdot 5 \\\\ {x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{x}^{3}y & =5{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{4})\\,dx & =\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{4} & ={x}^{5}+C \\\\ y & =x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435867 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435863 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435867 1069 "q-335274" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435867 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435867 1071 "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435867 1072 #uuid "73fd6309-052f-5dd1-8e4c-82525a25d454" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435867 1074 "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=2x$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2x\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+2x{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot y & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}}) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435868 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435864 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435868 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435865 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435868 1069 "q-335830" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435868 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435868 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(0)=4\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435868 1072 #uuid "eb095d57-a547-5e39-b061-eaeaefb98858" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true] [17592186435868 1074 "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2{e}^{-2x}\\cdot y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-2x} & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & ={e}^{2x}(C-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={e}^{2(0)}(C-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\ 4 & =C-1 \\\\ C & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$" 13194139534782 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" 17592186435831 "answer-0b978ec0-c1dc-593e-85ec-c512eb8b8bba" 17592186435832 "answer-12775c73-4492-5f55-9c3e-64f7ff76cc43" 17592186435833 "answer-1d921686-f16a-5dba-8a57-bf18cea65de9" 17592186435834 "answer-1da376ec-fadc-58b2-9050-98c3a0e3289d" 17592186435835 "answer-21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" 17592186435836 "answer-21b21254-3e18-5695-9053-f6ca9ce7117b" 17592186435837 "answer-39544074-ae02-530d-9e3a-2a0b0340a99a" 17592186435838 "answer-42485b83-5931-53b1-8e35-f51001ba1f8e" 17592186435839 "answer-856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" 17592186435840 "answer-89b946b2-2ff0-52e9